<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil down, meal firm.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil down, meal firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets in limited trading in a steady undertone, traders said.</p>
<p>They said arrivals were around 2,000 tonnes in central Indian markets.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell by 100 rupees per tonne on selling pressure from plants and limited local demand, traders said.</p>
<p>Volumes were low and the undertone easy, they said.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were firm on limited selling. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $284 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $112 per tonne in export and was 3,850-3,900 rupees per tonne in FOR condition. Volumes traded were poor in a steady undertone.</p>
